00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:28.560
I've gone off and counted all the
squares and it worked out to be 381

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:34.020
square centimeters. This converts to 0.76 mL of sunscreen for my face to

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:38.790
get 2 milligrams per square centimeter,
which is about 60% of a quarter of a

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:43.380
teaspoon, so somewhere between half a
teaspoon and two thirds. I'm converting

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.040
all of these to quarter teaspoons
because that's the most common small

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.150
measuring spoon that people tend to have.
I realized that I also apply sunscreen

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:57.750
to this area between my chin and where
it starts to turn into my neck and I

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.860
also measured that part using the tape
method. It worked out to be 75 square

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:08.670
centimeters which takes the total up to
about 3/4 of 1/4 tsp. I also apply

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:13.890
sunscreen with these three fingers which
works out to be 30 square centimeters

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:19.320
according to my tape method. That takes
it up to about a bit over three-quarters

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:23.130
of a quarter teaspoon. Obviously this
measurement is a bit flawed because I

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:27.030
probably end up with 10 layers of
sunscreen on these fingers but it's

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:30.780
probably about as good of an
approximation as I'm going to get. I've

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:35.460
also been meaning to wear sunscreen more
on my neck and my décolletage which turn

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.250
out to be 144 and 280 square

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:42.840
centimeters respectively, so this area
converts to about two thirds of a

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.370
quarter teaspoon. If you want to try this
